[],"ruleId":"Tabernacle::Tent of Meeting::reviewed_publisher_redirect","sourceHeadwordId":"TentofMeeting"},"text":"So Solomon went to Jerusalem from the high place in Gibeon, from before the Tent of Meeting, and he reigned over Israel.","verse":13}],"id":"Tabernacle","label":"Tent of Meeting","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Tabernacle::Tent of Meeting::reviewed_publisher_redirect","scope":"reviewed_publisher_redirect","senseReview":"The original publisher explicitly links this complete unambiguous name/phrase to this target. Redirect and target were reviewed once; actual BSB phrase and full word boundaries required. Target original title and complete article remain unchanged.","sourceHeadwordId":"TentofMeeting","term":"Tent of Meeting"}],"matchingRule":"source_verified_redirect","matchingRules":["source_verified_redirect"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Tabernacle","sourceTitle":"Tabernacle"},{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"Uri","senseEvidence":{"basis":"source_verse_citation","originalCitations":[{"anchorIndex":4,"href":"?bref=2Chr.1.5","rawReference":"2Chr.1.5"}],"ruleId":"Uri::Uri::source_verse_citation","sourceHeadwordId":"Uri"},"text":"But the bronze altar made by Bezalel son of Uri, the son of Hur, was in Gibeon before the tabernacle of the LORD. So Solomon and the assembly inquired of Him there.","verse":5}],"id":"Uri","label":"Uri","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Uri::Uri::source_verse_citation","scope":"source_verse_citation","senseReview":"Original complete headword and source opening identify a named person, people, or place. Promotion requires a capitalized whole name and the original article explicitly citing this same BSB verse. No arbitrary qualifier stripping or book-title inference. This citation-constrained rule was reviewed once globally; unmatched contexts remain excluded.","sourceHeadwordId":"Uri","term":"Uri"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Uri","sourceTitle":"Uri"},{"evidence":[{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"wealth","senseEvidence":{"basis":"source_verse_citation","originalCitations":[{"anchorIndex":4,"href":"?bref=2Chr.1.11-12","rawReference":"2Chr.1.11-12"}],"ruleId":"Wealth::Wealth::source_verse_citation","sourceHeadwordId":"Wealth"},"text":"God said to Solomon, “Since this was in your heart instead of requesting riches or wealth or honor for yourself or death for your enemies—and since you have not even requested long life but have asked for wisdom and knowledge to govern My people over whom I have made you king—","verse":11},{"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","phrase":"wealth","senseEvidence":{"basis":"source_verse_citation","originalCitations":[{"anchorIndex":4,"href":"?bref=2Chr.1.11-12","rawReference":"2Chr.1.11-12"}],"ruleId":"Wealth::Wealth::source_verse_citation","sourceHeadwordId":"Wealth"},"text":"therefore wisdom and knowledge have been granted to you. And I will also give you riches and wealth and honor unlike anything given to the kings before you or after you.”","verse":12}],"id":"Wealth","label":"wealth","matchReviews":[{"ruleId":"Wealth::Wealth::source_verse_citation","scope":"source_verse_citation","senseReview":"Reviewed original headword and source sense. This substantive word is admitted only where the original article explicitly cites the exact occurrence verse; ambiguous homographs and known context mismatches are separately excluded. This is selective contextual evidence, not an automatic rule for every same-spelling word.","sourceHeadwordId":"Wealth","term":"Wealth"}],"matchingRule":"reviewed_exact_headword","matchingRules":["reviewed_exact_headword"],"sourceProvenanceId":"Wealth","sourceTitle":"Wealth"}],"format":"bsb-study-chapter-v2","notes":[{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=2Chr.1.1","r":"2Chr.1.1","rawR":"2Chr.1.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.1.1","value":"2Chr.1.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"1:1"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," David had asked that the Lord be with ",{"c":["Solomon"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.22.11","r":"1Chr.22.11","rawR":"1Chr.22.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.22.11","value":"1Chr.22.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 22:11"},") and that Solomon be strong and of good courage (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.28.20","r":"1Chr.28.20","rawR":"1Chr.28.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.28.20","value":"1Chr.28.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 28:20"},"). David also declared that God would make Solomon great, giving strength to all Israel (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.29.12","r":"1Chr.29.12","rawR":"1Chr.29.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.29.12","value":"1Chr.29.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 29:12"},"). Three points about Solomon echo David’s blessings: Solomon ",{"c":["took firm control of his kingdom"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},{"c":[","],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," . . . ",{"c":["God was with him"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},{"c":[","],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," and God ",{"c":["made him very powerful."],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:IIChr.1.1","refs":[{"book":"2CH","endChapter":1,"endVerse":1,"startChapter":1,"startVerse":1}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"IIChr.1.1","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"2CH","sourceChapterCoverage":[1],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"d0c076d06d6f301c5d5b68ce68037edba986fc7ae9155cb6e57f442ccb9d1825","sourceItemName":"IIChr.1.1","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":4895,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"2CH","canonicalOSIS":"2Chr","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"2Chr"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"2Chr.1.1","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"IIChr.1.1","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=2Chr.1.2-6","r":"2Chr.1.2-6","rawR":"2Chr.1.2-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.1.2-6","value":"2Chr.1.2-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"1:2-6"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," Solomon’s journey to ",{"c":["Gibeon"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},{"c":[","],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," reported in ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.3.4","r":"1Kgs.3.4","rawR":"1Kgs.3.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.3.4","value":"1Kgs.3.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 3:4"},", is here elaborated. This great public venture was closely associated with Solomon taking the throne. The event included military commanders and ",{"c":["clan leaders"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"},". It took place in Gibeon because the Tabernacle was there, as was the great ",{"c":["bronze altar"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," where sacrifices were regularly offered."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:IIChr.1.2-6","refs":[{"book":"2CH","endChapter":1,"endVerse":6,"startChapter":1,"startVerse":2}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"IIChr.1.2-6","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"2CH","sourceChapterCoverage":[1],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"02759852a27ec8d3ce8d013523c7350a7bb5155c36af83b5e5137c7ce26358c6","sourceItemName":"IIChr.1.2-6","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":4896,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"2CH","canonicalOSIS":"2Chr","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"2Chr"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"2Chr.1.2-6","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"IIChr.1.2-6","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=2Chr.1.3","r":"2Chr.1.3","rawR":"2Chr.1.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.1.3","value":"2Chr.1.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"1:3"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," ",{"c":["Tabernacle:"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," See ",{"href":"?item=Exod.27.21_StudyNote_Filament","id":"Exod.27.21_StudyNote_Filament","rawId":"Exod.27.21_StudyNote_Filament","t":"link","v":"study note on Exod 27:21"},"."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:IIChr.1.3","refs":[{"book":"2CH","endChapter":1,"endVerse":3,"startChapter":1,"startVerse":3}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"IIChr.1.3","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"2CH","sourceChapterCoverage":[1],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"807402faea7a099d1ed6b69bf313ef32ff71a196ba1b92176dc9f4b3955565dd","sourceItemName":"IIChr.1.3","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":4897,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"2CH","canonicalOSIS":"2Chr","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"2Chr"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"2Chr.1.3","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"IIChr.1.3","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=2Chr.1.7-12","r":"2Chr.1.7-12","rawR":"2Chr.1.7-12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.1.7-12","value":"2Chr.1.7-12"}],"t":"ref","v":"1:7-12"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," See “",{"href":"?item=SolomonsWisdom_ThemeNote_Filament","id":"SolomonsWisdom_ThemeNote_Filament","rawId":"SolomonsWisdom_ThemeNote_Filament","t":"link","v":"Solomon’s Wisdom"},"” Theme Note."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:IIChr.1.7-12","refs":[{"book":"2CH","endChapter":1,"endVerse":12,"startChapter":1,"startVerse":7}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"IIChr.1.7-12","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"2CH","sourceChapterCoverage":[1],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"09e4f29d49f8249eba06e49df67a3f47c56de7e21729a5ebcf3205866e5e7bb3","sourceItemName":"IIChr.1.7-12","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":4898,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"2CH","canonicalOSIS":"2Chr","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"2Chr"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"2Chr.1.7-12","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"IIChr.1.7-12","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=2Chr.1.10","r":"2Chr.1.10","rawR":"2Chr.1.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.1.10","value":"2Chr.1.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"1:10"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," Solomon received ",{"c":["wisdom and knowledge"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," so he could ",{"c":["govern"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," (Hebrew ",{"c":["shapat"],"sourceClass":"hebrew","t":"span"},") well. The word ",{"c":["shapat"],"sourceClass":"hebrew","t":"span"},{"c":[","],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," often rendered “judge” (e.g., in Judges), can also mean “govern.”"],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:IIChr.1.10","refs":[{"book":"2CH","endChapter":1,"endVerse":10,"startChapter":1,"startVerse":10}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"IIChr.1.10","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"2CH","sourceChapterCoverage":[1],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"33d366bad18132fcb330d37b84dfc98086219540aaadfe80f68cd40f3c2a6aa7","sourceItemName":"IIChr.1.10","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":4899,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"2CH","canonicalOSIS":"2Chr","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"2Chr"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"2Chr.1.10","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"IIChr.1.10","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=2Chr.1.14-17","r":"2Chr.1.14-17","rawR":"2Chr.1.14-17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.1.14-17","value":"2Chr.1.14-17"}],"t":"ref","v":"1:14-17"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," The illustration of Solomon’s wealth and power (expanded on in ",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.9.25-28","r":"2Chr.9.25-28","rawR":"2Chr.9.25-28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.9.25-28","value":"2Chr.9.25-28"}],"t":"ref","v":"9:25-28"},") comes from the summary of his kingdom in ",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.10.26-29","r":"1Kgs.10.26-29","rawR":"1Kgs.10.26-29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.10.26-29","value":"1Kgs.10.26-29"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 10:26-29"},". In Kings, the summary of Solomon’s wealth provided a transition to the negative aspects of Solomon’s rule (",{"href":"?bref=1Kgs.11.1-43","r":"1Kgs.11.1-43","rawR":"1Kgs.11.1-43","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Kgs.11.1-43","value":"1Kgs.11.1-43"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Kgs 11"},"). Here, Solomon’s amassing of wealth showed the fulfillment of God’s promise (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.1.12","r":"2Chr.1.12","rawR":"2Chr.1.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.1.12","value":"2Chr.1.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 1:12"},")."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:IIChr.1.14-17","refs":[{"book":"2CH","endChapter":1,"endVerse":17,"startChapter":1,"startVerse":14}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"IIChr.1.14-17","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"2CH","sourceChapterCoverage":[1],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"e382513ad7dd789bc0cf6afc1d847dba934ac0a2907704eb74ab7c5034059f30","sourceItemName":"IIChr.1.14-17","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":4900,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"2CH","canonicalOSIS":"2Chr","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"2Chr"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"2Chr.1.14-17","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"IIChr.1.14-17","type":"StudyNote"},{"chapterAssociationStatus":"canonical_reference","content":[{"c":[{"c":[{"href":"?bref=2Chr.1.16","r":"2Chr.1.16","rawR":"2Chr.1.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.1.16","value":"2Chr.1.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"1:16"}],"sourceClass":"sn-ref","t":"span"}," If ",{"c":["Egypt"],"sourceClass":"sn-excerpt","t":"span"}," is the correct translation, this verse indicates disobedience by Solomon (see ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.17.16","r":"Deut.17.16","rawR":"Deut.17.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.17.16","value":"Deut.17.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Deut 17:16"},"). However, importing from ",{"c":["Muzur"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," in Anatolia was not prohibited."],"sourceClass":"sn-text","t":"p"}],"id":"StudyNote:IIChr.1.16","refs":[{"book":"2CH","endChapter":1,"endVerse":16,"startChapter":1,"startVerse":16}],"sourceAttributes":{"name":"IIChr.1.16","product":"TyndaleOpenStudyNotes","typename":"StudyNote"},"sourceBookAppCode":"2CH","sourceChapterCoverage":[1],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"f8e8cf85575a39063e1739767b9757c7e0cec54f109ef29e3666ce7e30d39cd4","sourceItemName":"IIChr.1.16","sourceMember":"Tyndale Open Study Notes/StudyNotes.xml","sourceOrder":4901,"sourceReferenceException":false,"sourceReferenceMappingEvidence":{"appCode":"2CH","canonicalOSIS":"2Chr","method":"official_book_intro_ref_title","sourceOSIS":"2Chr"},"sourceReferenceStatus":"canonical","sourceRefsExact":"2Chr.1.16","sourceRelease":"1.25","sourceTitleExact":null,"supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[],"title":"IIChr.1.16","type":"StudyNote"}],"version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}